# =====================================================================
# 1.x Stable — current and forward path
# =====================================================================

# ---------- 1.0.x Baseline ----------
# 1.0.0   Stable ABI + server set (init / console / ping)
# 1.0.y   Bugfixes only — no new feature series
#
# Acceptance today: QEMU smoke (banner, canopy, pong, init exit).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1.1.x  Process model + dynamic ELF
# Goal: start a new U-task from an ELF image at runtime (not only boot embed).
# ABI: additive (e.g. SYS_SPAWN / task caps). No Linux execve semantics.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Work to land before tagging 1.1.0 (track in PRs; do not bump VERSION each step):
#   W1  Per-task page tables (or ASID-ready root); switch satp on context switch
#   W2  Map ELF PT_LOAD + stack into the child AS; inherit/mint minimal CSpace
#   W3  Kernel or privileged server API to create task from ELF bytes / embedded blob
#   W4  Wait/reap or zombie harvest for children; ledger events for spawn/exit
#   W5  Smoke: init (or a tiny launcher) spawns a hello ELF and sees it exit
#
# Releases:
# 1.1.0   Series usable: spawn ELF + per-task AS
# 1.1.y   Loader / spawn / AS bugfixes only
#
# Out of scope for 1.1: shell UI, filesystem paths to ELF, Linux ELF ABI quirks
# beyond what riscv64 ET_EXEC already needs.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1.2.x  Console I/O + interactive shell
# Goal: type commands on the QEMU serial; shell parses and spawns programs.
# Shell = small DeepRoot-native ELF (builtins + spawn); not bash/dash/BusyBox.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Work to land before tagging 1.2.0:
#   W1  Console server (or kernel) provides blocking read of UART + write
#       via IPC or thin syscalls; line discipline enough for CR/LF + backspace
#   W2  Cap / endpoint so only designated tasks own the console
#   W3  user/shell: prompt, read line, split argv, builtins (help, yield, exit)
#   W4  Shell uses 1.1 spawn to run another embedded or known ELF (e.g. ping)
#   W5  init starts shell instead of (or after) one-shot ping/console demo flow
#   W6  Smoke: scripted QEMU input runs `help` / spawn and greps output
#
# Releases:
# 1.2.0   Interactive shell on serial + spawn from shell
# 1.2.y   Editing / builtins / console IPC fixes only
#
# Out of scope for 1.2: scripts from disk, pipes/redirection (may stub), POSIX sh.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1.3.x  Filesystem
# Goal: path-based open/read/write; shell can run /bin/... or read files.
# FS lives in userspace as a server; kernel only mediates caps + IPC (+ maybe
# a Frame/page grant). Still not a Linux VFS.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Work to land before tagging 1.3.0:
#   W1  FS IPC protocol in deeproot-abi (open/close/read/write/readdir or minimal)
#   W2  ramfs server first (in-memory tree); seed with hello / shell / ping blobs
#   W3  File / Dir caps or badge+path; rights READ/WRITE enforced
#   W4  Shell: `ls`, `cat`, run program by path (load ELF bytes via FS then spawn)
#   W5  Optional stretch in same series only if still small: virtio-blk backend
#       behind the same FS protocol (otherwise defer to 1.4)
#   W6  Smoke: boot → shell → cat file → spawn ELF from ramfs
#
# Releases:
# 1.3.0   ramfs ls/cat for shell
# 1.3.y   FS protocol / ramfs / path fixes only
#
# Out of scope for 1.3: full Unix permissions model, many FS types, mmap files.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1.4.x  Block / console devices behind existing servers
# Goal: real virtio (or similar) backends without changing the 1.1–1.3 user model.
# Only start when 1.3 is solid.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Work to land before tagging 1.4.0:
#   W1  virtio-blk (or equivalent) behind the FS protocol — persist beyond ramfs
#   W2  virtio-console or cleaner UART path for the console server (if needed)
#   W3  Smoke: boot from/with block-backed FS or read a file from virtio-blk
#
# Releases:
# 1.4.0   Ramdisk block stand-in on boot path (DISK + read)
# 1.4.1   DRFS image on ramdisk; shell ls/cat serve block text
# 1.4.y   Small block/FS fixes only (virtio-blk proper → 1.6)
#
# Out of scope for 1.4:
#   networking, SMP production, GPU desktop, Linux syscall compat, multi-user login.
# Forward path continues in 1.5+ below (through 2.0).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
